        "texts": {
          "summary": "FeatureMatrix (memo) re-renders with 80 FeatureRow below it twice on every click: prop `labels` is a new object each render with the same value, created at PricingPage.tsx:26. Wasted: about 27.4 ms per click. Fix: move it out of the component, since it uses nothing from it, or wrap it in useMemo (React Compiler would do this automatically).",
          "why": "memo only skips a render when every prop is the same object as last time. `labels` looks the same, but it's a new object on every render, so FeatureMatrix and everything below it re-renders for nothing.",
          "line": "`labels={{ included: 'Included', missing: 'Not included' }}` at PricingPage.tsx:26.",
          "fix": "It uses nothing from the component, so move it outside, to the top of the file: `const LABELS = { included: 'Included', missing: 'Not included' };`, then pass `labels={LABELS}`. FeatureMatrix then gets the same object on every render. Wrapping it in useMemo also works: `const labels = useMemo(() => ({ included: 'Included', missing: 'Not included' }), []);`. React Compiler would do this automatically."
        },
        "rank": 1
